1. using the web interface at github.com made a fork of ThePacielloGroup/cupper repo into MaxWhitney/deceptive_design_scrape.
2. Using desktop github tool cloned MaxWhitney/deceptive_design_scrape to local GitHub/deceptive_design_scrape, select the option to use the repo fork 'For my own purposes' not in order to 'To contribute to the parent project'.
3. Clicked the 'Fetch origin' button to download a copy to local storage.
4. Checked it out ..... looks good in deceptive_design_scrape folder

so now start repeating actions you did yesterday when you were working through the cupper install basics.

1. So interesting!! the only terminal window where 
    nvm -v
    npm -v
    node -v
return values is the terminal in which I installed nvm and npm yesterday! This may be because this is the only terminal window I restarted post installation, so it's the only with the appropriate env variables. Opening a fresh term now to test that theory. Yep, that's it. The other two term windows I'm working in predate the install of nvm. Okay, back to cupper set up, following the steps at https://thepaciellogroup.github.io/cupper/patterns/installation/. 
1. Check node and npm install:
    nvm -v returns 0.41.0
    npm -v returns 11.20.0
    node -v returns v26.13.1
2. ThePacielloGroup/cupper repo has already been forked and brought down locally into 'deceptive_design_scrape' folder/repo
3. from deceptive_design_scrape/ run 'npm install'
   note agin '12 vulnerabilities (3 moderate, 9 high)' is reported and I'm choosing not to attempt to patch because I will not be running node for any external user.
4. from deceptive_design_scrape/ run 'npm run clean'
5. modify the config.toml file
   cat config.toml 
        languageCode = "en-us"
        title = "Deceptive Design Scrape"
        baseURL = "https://example.org"
        canonifyURLs = true
        theme = "cupper"
        publishDir = "docs"

        [params]
          description = "Deceptive Design Scrape in support of bringing the material back under the Superbloom umbrella using **Cupper** customization of Hugo."
          codePenUser = "PenUserShouldNotBeTheRealHumanHeydon" 
6. There is no static/manifest.json, so modifications made there 
7. copy in logo.svg and placeholder png and svg to static/images

Customize in the most minor way
1. in content/_index.md set the title and minorly edit the content.
2. in content/patterns/pattern.md set the title, no edits to the conten

Build and view
1. from deceptive_design_scrape run 'npm run serve'
2. open the site using a browser at http://localhost:1313
Success!

Build to gitpages ....
1. Cupper created a /docs folder containing the last version of the site. I examined /docs and yep it looks good. 
2. Theoretically the github pages version will be at: https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape
    Presently that url 404s
3. Cupper docs state: add this value to your config.toml file as the baseURL. So doing that now. 
    vi config.toml
    baseURL = "https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape"

2. open the site using a browser at http://localhost:1313
Success!

